64,-10.0574],"date":"6 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 6: 608 km towards the Sahara."},{"name":"Smara","place":"Smara","at":[26.7436,-11.6645],"date":"7 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 7: 489 km into Western Sahara."},{"name":"El Ghallaouiya","place":"El Ghallaouiya","at":[21.5936,-10.6016],"date":"8 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 8: 628 km into Mauritania; stage 9 was a loop around El Ghallaouiya."},{"name":"Atar","place":"Atar","at":[20.5182,-13.0544],"date":"10 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 10: 440 km to Atar, then a rest day."},{"name":"Nouakchott","place":"Nouakchott","at":[18.0792,-15.978],"date":"12 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 11: 508 km to the Mauritanian capital."},{"name":"Tidjikdja","place":"Tidjikdja","at":[18.5545,-11.4326],"date":"13 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 12: 654 km east; stage 13 looped around Tidjikdja."},{"name":"Tichit","place":"Tichit","at":[18.4441,-9.4931],"date":"15 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 14: 234 km to the old caravan town of Tichit."},{"name":"Néma","place":"Néma","at":[16.6173,-7.2664],"date":"16 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 15: 499 km to Néma."},{"name":"Bamako","place":"Bamako","at":[12.6133,-7.985],"date":"17 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 16: 776 km into Mali."},{"name":"Bakel","place":"Bakel","at":[14.905,-12.4568],"date":"18 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 17: 804 km into Senegal."},{"name":"Tambacounda","place":"Tambacounda","at":[13.8686,-13.319],"date":"19 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 18: 292 km to Tambacounda."},{"name":"Dakar","place":"Dakar","at":[14.6934,-17.4479],"date":"21 Jan 2001","text":"Stage 19 reached Dakar on 20 January and a final loop ran on the 21st. Jutta Kleinschmidt and Andreas Schulz won in a Mitsubishi Pajero, the first woman to win the Dakar; Fabrizio Meoni won the bikes for KTM."}],"legs":[{"by":"ride","km":633,"line":[[48.8589,2.32],[43.1838,3.0042]]},{"by":"ride","km":436,"line":[[43.1838,3.0042],[39.986,-0.0377]]},{"by":"ride","km":399,"line":[[39.986,-0.0377],[36.8686,-2.312]]},{"by":"ferry","km":197,"line":[[36.8686,-2.312],[35.1736,-2.9368]]},{"by":"ride","km